<h2 id=3D"faq">FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q1. Should I use <code>-r</code> or <code>-vf fps=3DN</code>?</s=
trong><br>
A. Use <code>-vf fps=3DN</code> when in doubt. It references timestamps and=
 produces stable results especially with VFR sources like smartphone or OBS=
 recordings. Use <code>-r</code> for simple, constant frame rate sources.</=
p>
<p><strong>Q2. Does increasing the frame rate make motion smoother?</strong=
><br>
A. No =E2=80=94 the <code>fps</code> filter <strong>duplicates existing fra=
mes</strong>. Motion smoothness stays the same as the original. For genuine=
 interpolation (generating new in-between frames via motion estimation), us=
e the <code>minterpolate</code> filter =E2=80=94 but it=E2=80=99s significa=
ntly slower.</p>
<p><strong>Q3. How do I verify the output frame rate after conversion?</str=
ong></p>
<div class=3D"pre-wrapper"><pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark" style=3D"b=
ackground-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" da=
ta-language=3D"bash"><code><span class=3D"line"><span style=3D"color:#B392F=
0">ffprobe</span><span style=3D"color:#79B8FF"> -v</span><span style=3D"col=
or:#9ECBFF"> error</span><span style=3D"color:#79B8FF"> -select_streams</sp=
an><span style=3D"color:#9ECBFF"> v:0</span><span style=3D"color:#79B8FF"> =
\</span></span>
<span class=3D"line"><span style=3D"color:#79B8FF">  -show_entries</span><s=
pan style=3D"color:#9ECBFF"> stream=3Davg_frame_rate</span><span style=3D"c=
olor:#79B8FF"> \</span></span>
<span class=3D"line"><span style=3D"color:#79B8FF">  -of</span><span style=
=3D"color:#9ECBFF"> default=3Dnoprint_wrappers=3D</span><span style=3D"colo=
r:#79B8FF">1</span><span style=3D"color:#9ECBFF"> output.mp4</span></span><=
/code></pre><button class=3D"copy-btn" aria-label=3D"Copy code">Copy</butto=
n></div>
<p><strong>Q4. Can I keep audio in a timelapse?</strong><br>
A. Technically yes, but the audio won=E2=80=99t sync with the shortened vid=
eo. The practical approach is to remove audio (<code>-an</code>) and add ba=
ckground music separately in post-production.</p>
